Generate {{ num_docs }} realistic English customer support ticket excerpts following these rules.

## Rules
- Each ticket must be independent with different customers and issues
- Mark PII entities with the following XML tags:
  - <PERSON>full name</PERSON>
  - <ADDRESS>full mailing address</ADDRESS>
  - <ORGANIZATION>company or institution name</ORGANIZATION>
  - <DATE_OF_BIRTH>date of birth</DATE_OF_BIRTH> (only when applicable, e.g., identity verification)
  - <BANK_ACCOUNT>bank account information (bank name, routing number, account number, account type)</BANK_ACCOUNT> (only when applicable, e.g., refunds)
- Text outside tags must be natural English prose
- Include both customer messages and agent responses
- Mix name formats: first-last, with middle initials, with titles, hyphenated, with apostrophes
- Addresses: full street address, city, state/province, postal code; mix US/UK/Canadian formats
- When date of birth appears, vary formats: "01/15/1990", "January 15, 1990", "1990-01-15", "15 Jan 1990"
- When bank account appears, include bank name + routing/ABA + account number + account type
- At least 30% of tickets should include identity verification with DATE_OF_BIRTH
- At least 30% of tickets should include refund/payment with BANK_ACCOUNT
- Each ticket should be 100-300 words

## Output format
Separate each ticket with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`

## Topic examples
- Billing dispute with refund to bank account, shipping address change request, account verification requiring date of birth, product return with company warehouse address, service cancellation with account holder verification